  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Just behind Toulon station, the Parc des Lices is a large city-centre green space redeveloped in 2026 by the City and the Métropole: meadows, a playground, a multisport court and a dog park dedicated to dogs. The city also says the dog area has an agility zone. A leash is compulsory in the municipality outside dog areas.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The city's page publishes no opening times; check with the town hall (04 94 36 30 00) or on site before timing your visit for late in the day. Stated sizes differ depending on the source (about 9 ha in a directory, nearly 9,200 m² for the redeveloped park according to the Métropole).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the dog park lets you safely let your dog off the leash; elsewhere in the park, a leash is required.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon station and the city centre are a short walk away, handy for combining the stroll with other stops during the day.</p>
